From 78256e8e00750b5f3270c5dce2e6752b5c1b74ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report a same-family code as a wrong code, not a miss
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Z77.9 entered for Z77.8 was reported as 'Missed Z77.8', and Z77.9 was
named nowhere unless the coder had also over-coded. Unmatched key codes
now pair with an unmatched coder code of the same family (ICD-10-CM
category, PCS section/body system/root operation, CPT first four) and
are reported as Wrong_Code with both codes — in grading feedback for
SDx, PCS and CPT and on the review screen and export. PCS names the
character that differs. Scores do not change.

This also brings the Specificity Drops analytics to secondary
diagnoses, which it only ever counted on Wrong_Code rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GAgNTxNNybv6W7GXL33G6z
